'''Kimcang Baliscans''' ({{Langx|bl|Kimkang-Baliscano}}; {{langx|vi|Người Kim Cảng Balisca}}) are [[Baliscans|Baliscan citizens]] of full or partial [[Kimcang]] ancestry. They constitute one of the oldest, largest, and most integrated Fosian communities within the [[Baliscan Confederation]]. According to the [[2025 Baliscan census]], there were 1,248,735 individuals identifying as Kimcang Baliscan, inclusive of those identifying with multiple ethnicities.

While limited ties existed during the [[Colonial Balisca|colonial period]] through trade links with the [[Sultanate of Maros]], the community's primary demographic foundation was laid during the massive state-sponsored resettlement of refugees following the end of the [[Great Adonian War]]. Due to Balisca's geopolitical stance of "active non-alignment" and its historical ideological sympathy with anti-colonial movements, the Confederation became a primary destination for Indochinese refugees in the Western Hemisphere.

